{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793885270,"nonce":"s/IUIUQiI/kkrxjeCueSeRLv4jY=","message":"Owner-requested debug-only CSS file hot reload is checkpointed in c44e21019722cd97ba5222abd9d47df370af9e42.\n\nThe new opt-in css-hot-reload feature is forwarded by the blinc facade and does not enable Subsecond/dx. WindowedContext::watch_css(name, path) loads and replaces a named source through set_css; unwatch_css stops watching while retaining its CSS. Native debug watchers debounce saves, handle atomic replacement, suppress unchanged contents, retain the last valid stylesheet after read/parse errors, and wake the existing scheduler. Watches are context-owned and stop on close. The frame loop consumes updates and invalidates cached rendering using the existing full CSS/layout scheduling. Release/web/mobile implementations perform no file reads or watching. Embedded set_css remains the release stylesheet.\n\nScoped evidence: all six native filesystem/scheduler/layout tests pass on Mac and Linux NUC, with no skips. Coverage includes repeated saves, atomic saves, empty/removal/invalid files and recovery, unchanged/unrelated writes, duplicate registration, failed retargeting, context/source isolation, cleanup, root variables, removed rules, Signal persistence and restyling the existing render tree. Mac actual release test passes; NUC passes the same guard with debug_assertions disabled for blinc_app only. Both guard tests retain the stylesheet and succeed with an absent file path. Facade wasm32 web+css-hot-reload compilation, scoped rustfmt/whitespace and mdBook pass.\n\nNUC ran from /home/raikage/.cache/blinc-css-reload-20261105.N41umn, separate from owner work. Seven tested source/manifest hashes match the Mac checkpoint. Missing build prerequisites were extracted into a private SDK; no system packages or owner checkout were modified. Dependency versions were retained while pruning absent generated examples from its copied lockfile. This was filesystem/scheduler/layout testing, not a NUC GPU/performance claim. Local evidence: /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-native-final.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-release.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-web.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-nuc-debug-final.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-nuc-release-guard.log and /private/tmp/blinc-css-reload-nuc-source-hashes.json.\n\nPublic book setup and facade feature table updated. Status remains open for release review; no publish/push/closure.","files":null}]}